redis
------------------------------------------
Redis is an in-memory data structure store, used as a database, cache and
message broker. It supports data structures such as strings, hashes, lists,
sets, sorted sets with range queries, bitmaps, hyperloglogs, geospatial indexes
with radius queries and streams. Redis has built-in replication, Lua scripting,
LRU eviction, transactions and different levels of on-disk persistence, and
provides high availability via Redis Sentinel and automatic partitioning with
Redis Cluster.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libxxhash0-0.8.4-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.13-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libxxhash-devel-0.8.4-1
  make-4.4.1-2
  tcl-8.6.12-1

Canonical website:
  https://redis.io/

Canonical download:
  http://download.redis.io/releases/redis-8.12.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack redis-8.12.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./redis-8.12.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/redis-8.12.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/redis-8.12.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

